  "worked_solution": "The function has a discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote at $x=0.$ Note that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty ,\n$$\n\nwhich is enough to conclude that there is a discontinuity due to a vertical asymptote at $x=0.$ \n\nThere are also discontinuities at $x=1$ and $x=3,$ but they are not discontinuities due to vertical asymptotes.",
